      "date": "2026-05-06T11:56:32.000Z",
      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings: EPS and revenues miss analyst expectations",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹15.63 (down from ₹16.71 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹175.1b (up 96% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹4.13b (down 6.5% from FY 2025). Profit margin: 2.4% (down from 5.0% in FY 2025). The decrease in margin was driven by higher expenses. Revenue missed analyst estimates by 2.8%. Earnings per share (EPS) also missed analyst estimates by 20%. Revenue is expected to decline by 21% p.a. on average during the next 2 years, while revenues in the Beverage industry in India are expected to grow by 11%. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 12% per year but the company’s share price has only increased by 1% per year, which means it is significantly lagging earnings growth.",
